<title>FINLAND: CASTRUM SAYS 1997 PROFIT POSSIBLE.</title>
<headline>CASTRUM SAYS 1997 PROFIT POSSIBLE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish real estate investment company Castrum Oy said on Tuesday the sale of shares in Julius Tallberg would make possible a positive 1997 result.</p>
<p>&quot;The gain from the sale of (15.68 percent of) shares in Julius Tallberg Kiinteistot in March will make possible a positive annual result with the current cost and interest rate level,&quot; it said in a statement with its 1996 results.</p>
<p>The company's loss narrowed to 13.5 million markka before extraordinary items in 1996 from a 24.7 million loss in 1995.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
